meeting|planned-gathering|NOUN|Gathering for discussion|An arranged occasion when people come together to discuss something.|cuộc họp; cuộc gặp để thảo luận|Our meeting about the school garden lasted forty minutes.|Cuộc họp của chúng tôi về khu vườn trường kéo dài bốn mươi phút.|Meeting is countable; hold a meeting describes arranging it and attend a meeting describes being present.|meeting
thank|express-gratitude|VERB|Express gratitude|Tell someone that you appreciate something they have done.|cảm ơn ai|Hoa thanked the librarian for finding the missing book.|Hoa cảm ơn thủ thư vì đã tìm được cuốn sách bị thất lạc.|Use thank someone for a noun or an -ing form; the person is the direct object.|thank
ferry|passenger-boat|NOUN|Boat for a regular crossing|A boat that transports passengers, and sometimes vehicles, across a stretch of water on a regular route.|phà; tàu chở khách hoặc xe qua một vùng nước|The last ferry left the island before sunset.|Chuyến phà cuối cùng rời đảo trước lúc mặt trời lặn.|Ferry is countable, with plural ferries; take a ferry refers to travelling on one.|ferry
town|settlement|NOUN|Urban settlement|A place with homes and businesses, generally larger than a village but smaller than a city.|thị trấn|The town opened a new playground beside its market.|Thị trấn mở một sân chơi mới bên cạnh chợ.|Town is countable; in town can refer to the local central area, while in a town names a settlement.|town
reading|written-text-activity|NOUN|Activity involving written words|The activity of looking at written words and understanding their meaning.|việc đọc; hoạt động đọc văn bản|An hour of reading helped Bao learn about ocean life.|Một giờ đọc sách giúp Bảo tìm hiểu về sinh vật đại dương.|Reading is uncountable when it names an activity; use do some reading rather than a reading for this sense.|reading
roast|dry-heat-cooking|VERB|Cook with dry heat|Cook food using dry heat, usually inside an oven or above a fire.|nướng bằng nhiệt khô, thường trong lò hoặc trên lửa|We roasted carrots with garlic for the evening meal.|Chúng tôi nướng cà rốt với tỏi cho bữa tối.|Roast takes the food as its object; roasted can describe food prepared this way.|roast
popular|liked-by-many|ADJECTIVE|Liked by many|Liked, enjoyed or chosen by a large number of people.|được nhiều người yêu thích; được ưa chuộng|The new swimming pool is popular with local families.|Bể bơi mới được các gia đình địa phương yêu thích.|Use popular with a group of people and popular in a place; popularity does not itself prove quality.|popular
building|roofed-structure|NOUN|Constructed structure|A structure with walls and a roof, used for living, working or other activities.|tòa nhà; công trình có tường và mái|A brick building shelters the village's fire engine.|Một tòa nhà bằng gạch là nơi để xe cứu hỏa của làng.|Building is countable in this sense; tall building and office building identify physical structures.|building
tram|street-rail-vehicle|NOUN|Electric street rail vehicle|An electric vehicle that carries passengers along rails, often laid in city streets.|tàu điện chạy trên đường ray trong phố|A yellow tram stopped outside the theatre.|Một chiếc tàu điện màu vàng dừng bên ngoài nhà hát.|Tram is countable; by tram describes the means of transport and on a tram describes being aboard.|tram
agree|same-opinion|VERB|Share an opinion|Have the same opinion as another person about something.|đồng tình; có cùng ý kiến|I agree with Thu that the path needs better lighting.|Tôi đồng tình với Thu rằng lối đi cần được chiếu sáng tốt hơn.|Use agree with a person or an opinion, or agree that followed by a clause.|agree
agree|accept-plan|VERB|Accept an arrangement|Say that you are willing to accept a proposed action or arrangement.|đồng ý; chấp thuận làm việc gì|The neighbours agreed to share the cost of a new fence.|Những người hàng xóm đồng ý chia sẻ chi phí làm hàng rào mới.|Use agree to do for accepting an action; agree on something can describe reaching a shared decision.|agree
meal|eating-occasion|NOUN|Occasion for eating|An occasion when food is eaten, or the food eaten on that occasion.|bữa ăn; thức ăn dùng trong một bữa|We prepared a simple meal for the tired travellers.|Chúng tôi nấu một bữa đơn giản để mời những người đi đường mệt mỏi.|Meal is countable; have a meal and eat a meal both refer to eating at one occasion.|meal
piano|keyboard-instrument|NOUN|Keyboard instrument with strings|A musical instrument whose keys operate hammers that strike strings.|đàn piano; đàn dương cầm|The old piano was tuned before the students' recital.|Chiếc đàn piano cũ được chỉnh dây trước buổi biểu diễn của học sinh.|Piano is countable; play the piano is a standard expression for performing on this instrument.|piano
pollute|contaminate-environment|VERB|Contaminate the environment|Make air, water or land harmful or dirty by adding unwanted substances.|gây ô nhiễm đất, nước hoặc không khí|Discarded batteries can pollute the soil around a rubbish dump.|Pin bị vứt bỏ có thể gây ô nhiễm đất quanh một bãi rác.|Pollute is transitive; use pollute a place or substance, optionally followed by with to name the pollutant.|pollute
tea|leaf-drink|NOUN|Drink prepared from leaves|A drink made by leaving dried tea leaves in hot water.|trà; nước uống pha từ lá trà|The host poured warm tea into small ceramic cups.|Chủ nhà rót trà ấm vào những chiếc chén gốm nhỏ.|Tea is normally uncountable as a drink; a tea can mean a serving in a café.|tea
guitar|string-instrument|NOUN|Plucked string instrument|A musical instrument with a long neck and strings played by plucking or strumming.|đàn ghi-ta|Linh carried her guitar to the rehearsal room.|Linh mang đàn ghi-ta của mình đến phòng tập.|Guitar is countable; play the guitar names the activity and acoustic or electric describes a type.|guitar
jungle|dense-tropical-forest|NOUN|Dense tropical forest|A forest in a hot, wet region where plants grow thickly together.|rừng rậm nhiệt đới|The research team followed a narrow trail through the jungle.|Nhóm nghiên cứu đi theo một lối mòn hẹp xuyên qua rừng rậm nhiệt đới.|Use a jungle for a particular forest or jungle without an article when describing vegetation or terrain generally.|jungle
understand|grasp-meaning|VERB|Grasp meaning|Know what words, information or an explanation mean.|hiểu ý nghĩa hoặc nội dung|After the demonstration, I understood the safety instructions.|Sau buổi hướng dẫn thực hành, tôi đã hiểu các chỉ dẫn an toàn.|The past and past participle are understood; understand can take a noun or a clause as its object.|understand
understand|recognize-feelings|VERB|Recognize another's feelings|Recognize why someone feels or behaves in a particular way.|thấu hiểu cảm xúc hoặc cách hành xử của ai|Nhi understands why her brother feels nervous before a match.|Nhi thấu hiểu vì sao anh trai mình cảm thấy lo lắng trước một trận đấu.|Use understand someone or understand how or why followed by a clause; this need not mean agreeing with their actions.|understand
bored|lack-interest|ADJECTIVE|Feeling uninterested|Feeling unhappy or restless because nothing holds your interest.|cảm thấy buồn chán|The children were bored by the repetitive guessing game.|Bọn trẻ cảm thấy chán vì trò đoán lặp đi lặp lại.|Bored describes the person experiencing the feeling; boring describes what causes it.|bored
tutor|individual-teacher|NOUN|Teacher offering personal lessons|A teacher who gives individual or small-group lessons, often as extra help.|gia sư; người dạy kèm|The tutor explained fractions using slices of an apple.|Gia sư giải thích phân số bằng những miếng táo.|Tutor is countable; a tutor in a subject or a maths tutor identifies the area taught.|tutor
nurse|healthcare-professional|NOUN|Professional who cares for patients|A trained healthcare worker who looks after people who are ill or injured.|y tá; điều dưỡng chăm sóc người bệnh hoặc bị thương|The nurse changed the bandage gently.|Người điều dưỡng nhẹ nhàng thay băng.|Nurse is countable and does not specify gender; nurses can work in hospitals, clinics or other care settings.|nurse
